From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: the HTML application object (<HTA:APPLICATION>) (9608)

HTML applications read their command line from their
<HTA:APPLICATION ID="oHTA"> element (oHTA.commandLine) and set their
window with its attributes (BORDER, CAPTION, SYSMENU, MAXIMIZEBUTTON,
MINIMIZEBUTTON, SHOWINTASKBAR, WINDOWSTATE, ICON). The element was an
unknown one: commandLine was undefined (scripts that split it threw) and
the window ignored the attributes. In an application started by mshta the
element now has commandLine (mshta's command line, as given), and the
window takes the styles its attributes ask for once the document has the
element. SINGLEINSTANCE is not enforced.
---
